Description: MERLIN (Causal Heterogeneity using Summary Statistics) is a unified 
    Bayesian framework that jointly estimates average and heterogeneity 
    effects using summary data from genome-wide association studies (GWAS) and 
    Genome-Wide Interaction Studies (GWIS).
